   "q_en": "<p>The ratio between the angles of a quadrilateral is 7:5:2:6. If the difference between the largest and smallest angle of the quadrilateral is 25% more than one of the angles of a parallelogram, then what can be inferred about the largest angle of the parallelogram?</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:5:2:6 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "100",
    "108",
    "112.5",
    "115"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "100",
    "108",
    "112.5",
    "115"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "solution_en": "<p>The ratio between the angles of a quadrilateral is 7:5:2:6</p><p>The sum of the angles of the quadrilateral is 360 degrees.</p><p>Hence, 7x + 5x + 2x + 6x = 360</p><p>or 20x = 360</p><p>or x = 18 degrees.</p><p>Hence the angles are 126, 90, 36 and 108 degrees respectively.</p><p>Difference between the largest and smallest angle = 90 degrees.</p><p>Now that is 25% more than one of the angles of a parallelogram.</p><p>Thus one of the angles of a parallelogram is 72 degrees, and it's adjacent angle is 108 degrees.</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>The ratio between the angles of a quadrilateral is 7:5:2:6</p><p>The sum of the angles of the quadrilateral is 360 degrees.</p><p>Hence, 7x + 5x + 2x + 6x = 360</p><p>or 20x = 360</p><p>or x = 18 degrees.</p><p>Hence the angles are 126, 90, 36 and 108 degrees respectively.</p><p>Difference between the largest and smallest angle = 90 degrees.</p><p>Now that is 25% more than one of the angles of a parallelogram.</p><p>Thus one of the angles of a parallelogram is 72 degrees, and it's adjacent angle is 108 degrees.</p>",
   "marks": 1.0,
