   "q_en": "<p>A rhombus ABCD has the diagonals of length 16cm and 12 cm. What is the distance between its parallel lines?</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "19.2 cm",
    "38.4 cm",
    "9.6 cm",
    "10 cm"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "19.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;",
    "38.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;",
    "9.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;",
    "10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"
   ],
   "answer": 2,
   "solution_en": "<p><img width=340 height=196 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11918/image013.png\"></p><p>Since the diagonals of rhombus perpendicularly bisects each other</p><p>Side of rhombus = ((12/2)<sup>2</sup> + (16/2)<sup>2</sup>)<sup>1/2</sup> = (36 + 64)<sup>1/2</sup> = 10 cm</p><p>Area of the rhombus = &frac12; * product of diagonals = &frac12; * 16*12 = 96cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of rhombus = Side * distance between parallel lines</p><p>96cm<sup>2</sup> = 10*distance between parallel lines</p><p>Distance between parallel lines = 96/10 = 9.6cm</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p><img width=340 height=196 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11918/image013.png\"></p><p>Since the diagonals of rhombus perpendicularly bisects each other</p><p>Side of rhombus = ((12/2)<sup>2</sup> + (16/2)<sup>2</sup>)<sup>1/2</sup> = (36 + 64)<sup>1/2</sup> = 10 cm</p><p>Area of the rhombus = &frac12; * product of diagonals = &frac12; * 16*12 = 96cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of rhombus = Side * distance between parallel lines</p><p>96cm<sup>2</sup> = 10*distance between parallel lines</p><p>Distance between parallel lines = 96/10 = 9.6cm</p>",
   "marks": 1.0,
   "neg": 0.25
  },
