   "answer": 3,
   "solution_en": "<p>Let, the number of sides of two regular polygons be n<sub>1</sub> and n<sub>2</sub>.</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/n<sub>2 </sub>= 2/3</p><p>[(n<sub>1 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] + [(n<sub>2 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] = 1080&deg;</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub> -  2 + n<sub>2</sub>  -  2 = 1080/180 = 6</p><p>n<sub>1</sub> + n<sub>2 </sub>= 10</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>+ 3n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>5n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 2</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>= 4</p><p>So, n<sub>2 </sub>= 6</p><p>Exterior angle of one polygon = 360/4 = 90&deg;</p><p>Exterior angle of the other polygon = 360/6 = 60&deg;</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the number of sides of two regular polygons be n<sub>1</sub> and n<sub>2</sub>.</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/n<sub>2 </sub>= 2/3</p><p>[(n<sub>1 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] + [(n<sub>2 </sub>- 2)  X  180 ] = 1080&deg;</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub> -  2 + n<sub>2</sub>  -  2 = 1080/180 = 6</p><p>n<sub>1</sub> + n<sub>2 </sub>= 10</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>+ 3n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>5n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 10</p><p>n<sub>1</sub>/2 = 2</p><p>n<sub>1 </sub>= 4</p><p>So, n<sub>2 </sub>= 6</p><p>Exterior angle of one polygon = 360/4 = 90&deg;</p><p>Exterior angle of the other polygon = 360/6 = 60&deg;</p>",
